# 🌐 My Final Project — Simple Portfolio Page

A small, single-page HTML site built to practice the full **Git & GitHub
workflow** (branching, pull requests, issues, code review, and GitHub
Actions) as my bootcamp capstone.

> The content of the site doesn't matter — this repo exists to show a
> clean, real-world Git/GitHub workflow.

---

## 📁 Project structure

```
.
├── index.html                     # Main page
├── style.css                      # All styling (kept separate from HTML)
├── .gitignore                     # Files Git should ignore
├── .github/
│   └── workflows/
│       └── check.yml              # GitHub Actions workflow
└── README.md                      # This file
```



## 🛠 Built with

- HTML
- CSS

## ✅ What this repo demonstrates

- Meaningful, step-by-step commits
- Feature branches merged through Pull Requests
- An Issue opened and closed by a linked PR
- A code review comment before merging
- A working GitHub Actions check on every push

---

*Final Project — Git & GitHub Bootcamp*